var F=[
 ['Profile','Who is the examination licensing?','Topics are matched to the competency profile of a beginning Filipino physician and to the roles the examination tests: recognising the classic presentation, choosing the decisive test, starting first-line treatment and acting on emergencies. Profiling also extends to the examiners: examiner profiling studies each examiner’s field of expertise, professional emphasis and style of questioning to anticipate which areas, and what kind of items, are likely to be given weight.','What a newly licensed general physician is expected to know and do, with added weight on areas the examiner profile points to.','Subspecialty depth and material beyond first-contact practice.'],
 ['Relevance','Does it matter in Philippine practice?','Priority goes to the conditions that fill Philippine wards, emergency rooms, clinics and communities, including locally important infections such as tuberculosis, dengue, malaria and leptospirosis.','Diseases and problems a physician in the Philippines is likely to meet and must manage.','Rare conditions with little bearing on local practice.'],
 ['TOS-alignment','Is it in the blueprint, and how heavily?','Each topic is checked against the Table of Specifications: the weight given to each topic of a subject and the cognitive level expected, from remembering through creating.','Topics inside the blueprint, studied in proportion to their weight.','Off-blueprint material, however interesting.'],
 ['Recurrence','Does the concept keep coming back?','Some concepts reappear across topics and in many forms: classic vignettes, first-line and life-saving treatments, diagnostic cut-offs, look-alike diseases. These earn the most space.','High-yield concepts that recur and anchor other topics.','One-off details that rarely resurface.'],
 ['Currency','Is it current?','Criteria, drug choices and recommended regimens change. Topics are kept at their present form so that what is studied matches current standard references.','Current criteria, regimens and standards of care.','Superseded regimens and outdated criteria.'],
 ['Testability','Can it be asked with one best answer?','The last screen favours content with a clear deciding point: a defining finding, a cut-off, a first-line drug, a next step, or a contraindication that settles a clinical vignette.','Concepts with a defensible single best answer.','Vague or purely descriptive material that cannot discriminate.']
];
var FK=['#1F6FD0','#2E8B3A','#7B2FA6','#C2710C','#C0392B','#9B1B4A'];
